From: mscharged-port
Subject: Give the European goalie tackle launch a defined scale
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

In the European builds Goalie::HitAttackTarget leaves the impact scale unset
for the pursue-deke types it skips (4, 7 and a stale type): retail scales the
launch by whatever register f3 held (EU revision 2 at 0x80080620). Natively
that read is undefined, so it takes the USA value 1.0 (owner decision). The
European code keeps its own deke-type handling; only the USA build resets a
stale type.

diff --git a/src/Game/Goalie.cpp b/src/Game/Goalie.cpp
index 8ff4bfc..d8b199b 100644
--- a/src/Game/Goalie.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Goalie.cpp
@@ -4135,6 +4135,11 @@ void Goalie::HitAttackTarget(cFielder* pFielder, bool bParam)
             nlVec3Set(v3Velocity, m_m4WorldMatrix.m11, m_m4WorldMatrix.m12, m_m4WorldMatrix.m13);
 #if defined(VERSION_R4QE01) || defined(VERSION_R4QJ01) || defined(VERSION_R4QK01)
             float fScale = 1.0f;
+#elif defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+            // EU leaves the impact scale unset for the skipped deke types:
+            // retail scales the launch by whatever f3 held. Natively that read
+            // is undefined, so it takes the USA value.
+            float fScale = 1.0f;
 #else
             // EU leaves the impact scale unset for the skipped deke types.
             float fScale;
